+/// NEGATIVE CONTROL for poc_forge_nonzero_initial_data.
+///
+/// Same setup, but here the boundary AIR sends initial_data = 0 (honest), while
+/// the CPU-read dummy still receives 5 off the bus. This MUST fail: the memory
+/// bus is a logup permutation argument, so a receive of value 5 with no matching
+/// send of 5 unbalances the bus and the verifier rejects. This proves:
+///   (a) the bus value binding genuinely works (forging prev_data requires a
+///       matching send), and
+///   (b) the ONLY reason poc_forge_nonzero_initial_data passes is the missing
+///       initial_data == 0 constraint in VolatileBoundaryAir::eval. If the AIR
+///       constrained initial_data == 0, the forgery test would look exactly like
+///       this control and would also fail.
+#[test]
+fn neg_control_mismatched_initial_data_rejected() {
